Q: What is a pivot table?

“Pivot table” has **two common meanings** — say which one you mean in interviews.

────────────────────────────────────────
🔹 1) DB design: join / junction / bridge table
(also casually called “pivot table”, especially in Laravel)

Used for **many-to-many** relationships — an intermediate table storing the links.

Example:
Student (id, name)
Course  (id, title)

student_course  ← pivot/junction
- student_id (FK → student)
- course_id  (FK → course)
- optional: enrolled_at, grade, PRIMARY KEY(student_id, course_id)

One student → many courses
One course  → many students

JPA:
@ManyToMany
@JoinTable(
  name = "student_course",
  joinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "student_id"),
  inverseJoinColumns = @JoinColumn(name = "course_id")
)
private Set<Course> courses;

Interview wording:
“Prefer saying junction/join table for M2M; ‘pivot table’ is informal but understood.”

────────────────────────────────────────
🔹 2) Reporting: rows → columns (aggregation matrix)

Transform row values into columns for analytics/reporting.

Sales rows:
| Region | Month | Revenue |
| East   | Jan   | 1000    |
| West   | Jan   | 1500    |
| East   | Feb   | 1200    |
| West   | Feb   | 1300    |

Pivoted:
| Region | Jan  | Feb  |
| East   | 1000 | 1200 |
| West   | 1500 | 1300 |

MySQL style (no native PIVOT like SQL Server) — conditional aggregation:

SELECT
  region,
  SUM(CASE WHEN month = 'Jan' THEN revenue ELSE 0 END) AS Jan,
  SUM(CASE WHEN month = 'Feb' THEN revenue ELSE 0 END) AS Feb
FROM sales
GROUP BY region;

────────────────────────────────────────
✅ Summary

| Term                         | Meaning                                      |
| ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Pivot (DB design)            | Junction table for many-to-many              |
| Pivot (SQL/reporting)        | Turn row values into columns + aggregate     |

One-liner:
“In schema design, pivot usually means the M2M join table; in analytics, pivot means reshaping rows into columns.”
